# Matches at any depth: the model crate has its own target/ directory.
target/
Cargo.lock.orig
.erpaval/sessions/
# Terraform working state: the conformance stack is created and destroyed per
# run, so its state is never worth committing.
conformance/infra/.terraform/
conformance/infra/.terraform.lock.hcl
conformance/infra/terraform.tfstate*
# Python build and test artifacts from the client library.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
# The wheel and venv the typed-consumer gate builds. `microvms-py/microvms.pyi` is the one
# generated Python artifact that IS committed — it is the thing the drift gate compares
# against — but the wheel built to prove it reaches a checker through PEP 561 is scratch,
# and a 200 MB debug wheel is not something to offer a reviewer.
dist-wheel/
.venv-typed/
.venv-bindings/
# The napi-rs build outputs. `napi build --platform` writes the compiled addon plus a
# generated loader and type declarations beside `package.json`; all three are derived from
# `microvms-js/src/` and are rebuilt by `npm run build`, so committing them would commit one
# platform's binary into a repo other platforms clone.
microvms-js/*.node
microvms-js/index.js
microvms-js/index.d.ts
microvms-js/node_modules/
# One package directory per entry in `package.json`'s `napi.targets`, written by
# `napi create-npm-dirs` and filled by `napi artifacts`. Derived in full — name, `os`,
# `cpu`, `libc`, and the inherited license and repository all come from the root
# manifest — so the target list is the source and these are its output.
microvms-js/npm/
sbom/
docs/.repomix/
docs/.packets/
# The CodeGraph index: a derived SQLite database of this tree's symbols and edges,
# plus the running daemon's socket and pid. It is rebuilt from source by `codegraph
# index`, so committing it would commit one machine's 18 MB binary artifact — and a
# live unix socket and pid file, which are meaningless in any other checkout.
.codegraph/
# The documentation site's install and build output. `site/src/content/docs/` is the one
# that matters: it is GENERATED in full by `site/scripts/sync-docs.mjs` from `docs/` plus
# `site/authored/`, so committing it would put a second copy of every claim in the repo and
# make a reviewer decide whether a diff in it is the point of a change or the residue of
# one. It is also the copy an editor would reach for first, and the next build discards
# that edit with no diff to show for it.
site/node_modules/
site/dist/
site/.astro/
site/src/content/docs/
# The wire schema, copied out of docs/ so the site can serve it at a stable URL. The
# committed original is docs/schema.json, which a gate byte-compares against the daemon.
site/public/schema.json
# Lighthouse output and the typecheck-gate probe build, both produced by `mise run docs:gate`.
site/.lighthouseci/
site/dist-typecheck-probe/
